ed notes from the diarized transcript by following the process, rules, and format below.\n\nPROCESS (in order):\n1. Extract the distinct topics, decisions, and outcomes - ignore transcript order and who spoke.\n2. Cluster related points; merge duplicates.\n3. Rank topics by importance; keep at most 4, merging or dropping the rest. Never exceed 4.\n4. Per topic, make the single key outcome the first bullet; add a second only if essential (2 max).\n5. Write each heading as the conclusion when there is one ("Launch Slipped To Q3" beats "Timeline"), then render in the exact Markdown format.\n\nRULES:\n- Fidelity: preserve numbers, names, dates, and IDs exactly - never vague-ify. Attribute a speaker only when identity matters (commitment, strong opinion, objection, disagreement); else omit names.\n- Sub-points: optionally add sparse indented lines for rationale, constraints, disagreement, risks, or dependencies - these do not count toward the 2-point cap.\n- Cut: greetings, filler, repetition, jokes, false starts, off-topic talk.\n- Never: invent facts, owners, or deadlines; present proposals as decisions; or record advice no one voiced. Keep real uncertainty, disagreement, risks, and blockers.\n- Scope: output only the shape below - no extra Summary, Decisions, Next Steps, or Open Questions sections.\n\nFORMAT (Markdown):\n- Line 1: a level-1 heading with a concise title derived from the dominant topic - do not fabricate a formal name.\n- Topic headings use level-2 headings.\n- Main points use bullets; supporting details use nested bullets.\n\nOUTPUT SHAPE:\n\n# [Meeting Title]\n\n## [Topic or Outcome]\n- [Key outcome]\n- [Second point - only if essential]\n  - [Supporting detail - optional]',b="Extract concrete follow-up tasks as action items.\nAssign an owner only when the transcript makes the responsible person clear; otherwise use null.\nPrefer owner names that exactly match a known speaker name.",A="anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5",w="gemini-2-5-flash-genai",S="rift_hui